You can simply just start those programs right away.
There are instructions included in the programs themselves.
I also added comments on how it does stuff. I hope it's enough.

main.py is the SAT Solver (not optimized)
test.py generates all the possible combinations

I could have optimized main.py by making it consider
one branch at a time instead of all at the same time,
and probably introduced many more better techniques.
However, I prioritized readebility and simplicity.
(I also didn't want to think too hard on it)

Therefore, the most my program can handle quickly
is about 100 clauses. I used my test.py to check.
This is way worse than the millions that the other
SAT Solvers can handle (this makes me feel bad now).
